ArgoCD UI and CLI Overview

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m exploring the UI and CLI of Argo CD 🚀
Understanding both UI and CLI helps in managing applications efficiently in real-world DevOps environments.

🔹 ArgoCD Dashboard (UI)
 ArgoCD provides a web-based dashboard to manage applications visually.
From the dashboard, you can:
View application status (Healthy / Degraded)
Monitor sync status (Synced / OutOfSync)
Trigger manual sync or rollback
Visualize resources like pods, services, deployments
This makes it easy to track and manage deployments in real time.

🔹 CLI Commands
 ArgoCD also provides a powerful CLI for automation and scripting.
Common commands include:
Login to ArgoCD
Add Git repositories
Create applications
Sync applications

Example:
argocd login <server>
argocd app list
argocd app sync <app-name>

CLI is especially useful for CI/CD pipeline integration and automation tasks.

🔹 Application View
 The application view shows:
Application health status
Resource hierarchy
Deployment history
Sync details
It helps developers quickly identify issues and manage deployments effectively.

💡 Key Insight:
 ArgoCD UI provides visual control, while CLI enables automation and scripting, making both essential for DevOps workflows.
